## Outcome-blind amendment before dispatch

The initial unrun design inherited the prior calibration's correct-code/true and
flawed-code/false pairing. Free design review identified that the source program
could cue the finite truth label, weakening the output-requirement test. Preserve
that design as output-requirement-protocol-v0-unrun.md and its successful execution
gate as output-requirement-reference-gate.json. No model calls used it. The final
same_program design above removes this cue before any treatment outcome exists;
its live label and initial-view equality checks are recorded separately in
output-requirement-reference-gate-v1.json. All old calibration traces remain intact.
